#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1440.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229982} :activity/id #uuid "ecc6f7d5-a6a0-5418-9648-573635651982" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229982 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186230191 :tutorial/content "Matrix exponentials can be used for solving *inhomogeneous systems* of ODEs as well. Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix, and suppose we are given an initial condition $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$.\n\nOur goal is to derive the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system.\n\nFirst, we eliminate the *inhomogeneous term* by a change of variables. We define\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nand differentiate it using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =\\cancel{-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+\\cancel{A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate both sides from $t_0$ to $t$ and get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNext, since $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to the initial variable $\\mathbf{x}(t).$ To do that we multiply both sides by $e^{A(t-t_0)}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our IVP is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere the first term represents the solution of the corresponding *homogeneous system*, and the second term gives a particular solution of our *inhomogeneous system*.\n\nLet's see some concrete examples." :tutorial/id #uuid "ff1bfa7f-286f-5481-8170-effabae1aa53" :tutorial/math-academy-id 14524 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "2e2fe55d-42e2-5c03-89a2-e19a648504d7" :step/math-academy-id 589676 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229983}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229983 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229131 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228916 :question/id #uuid "e151cd67-cf96-5378-9380-e9960c1eb6b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-21722"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "95223ee8-46d8-58c2-9e3b-017adb2789e8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050221}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229663} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229675} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308688} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308692} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308695} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308696} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396516} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479848} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479854} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541124} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541149} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557281} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557289} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557325} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558563}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"} :step/id #uuid "77745a11-4271-51f5-b398-2f10162b46cb" :step/math-academy-id 589677 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229984}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229132 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228914 :question/id #uuid "3638fd11-5f61-5656-89c4-18ee0a4318ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-21720"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eca32dd-1563-55c6-b594-08588efd601b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049663}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229678} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308718} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308719} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308723} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308724} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308736} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396565} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396729} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495074} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495161} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512909} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512945} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535950}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System Using a Given Matrix Exponential"} :step/id #uuid "6314ffb3-c936-5a5a-b8eb-f9a041a7e1a1" :step/math-academy-id 589680 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229985}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229985 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229133 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228915 :question/id #uuid "c24150ed-748b-5069-9fc5-48d4e6deaef2" :question/math-academy-id "e-21721"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049952}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229662} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229683} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311584} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311585} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311588} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311589} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370330} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396735} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396755} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396771} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479869} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535981}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System"} :step/id #uuid "96c720fc-5ade-5920-b439-4021bbbc0586" :step/math-academy-id 589683}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186229257}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495193} :activity/id #uuid "b9d3e9cf-c6b8-5144-84b6-fb2bd0e11696" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495181 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b596b99-7294-5ff0-b898-15ee8d9ff660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494537} {:answer/id #uuid "a547dde1-3353-563d-9dc4-c26608fe2262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494695} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1db945-1bea-566f-ac8f-8accdd99a0c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494803} {:answer/id #uuid "e10e0aba-3ff2-54c6-8ed9-ecc46df06c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494853}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494695} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f5cfcb1-f43f-54aa-937a-52c96207e17b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e9f770d5-4f03-58ec-b9ae-bcbaf7705c59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335166" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)+4,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "06d91f07-0fea-5beb-aa8a-cd77b3e6a896" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495188}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495188 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb2b0c4a-5f41-51b1-b049-b17c6daa263c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396737} {:answer/id #uuid "4db61969-a679-5616-b6d7-9ef5595f083e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396738} {:answer/id #uuid "b001af69-f2b3-5389-9b56-04a143bc76e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396739} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa8e09b-3618-57a8-8bb5-285e3c3130c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396740}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396739} :answer-field/id #uuid "4423074f-337c-560f-b946-81a6f27cf80f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8b178c4-a799-5c62-8f72-1a528733ac9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396742} {:answer/id #uuid "c166c192-8884-511b-9ab3-520dfd369763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(0)=x(0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396743} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8f0ebe-1062-5726-b1bb-015c0a277f9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396744} {:answer/id #uuid "ec37eb47-c21a-54c2-aa96-bd95ec88139f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396745}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396743} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16ad664-1e3d-55f3-8058-30911f724f18" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b34ccb5-bae6-51a5-9118-171f36032915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396747} {:answer/id #uuid "927a0ce8-1c41-5bff-b199-ca47d4f3891f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396748} {:answer/id #uuid "d4332a13-7707-56e5-9d4c-f85171d9d42e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396749}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396748} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2d49272-d22a-5953-a915-b76fe91c045b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396746} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b5d015d-eaf2-5953-a208-79b9f37e4968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396751} {:answer/id #uuid "30eef7f5-8b22-5be9-9b66-818bc874eb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396752} {:answer/id #uuid "1f580aa1-90f1-5a47-b37e-9bf7b327dcaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396753} {:answer/id #uuid "5548b470-04df-52fd-9078-8aee9471580b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396754}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396753} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b821195-ec1a-56fc-95c0-6d1616e5c0a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b0202c33-02b6-54b1-9971-6d025f9fe504" :question/math-academy-id "q-335401" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y(0)=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y(0)=x(0).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).$"} :step/id #uuid "2231ccca-1dd5-57de-b365-dbd0a5f43637" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495250}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495193 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c139fc5d-402e-5c97-b048-caf60e14b36c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306955} {:answer/id #uuid "6963f53e-90b3-59a4-b3ac-6bc885da9965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-\\cos(2t)+2\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494533}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494533} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b933995-aeb2-5960-92c8-2edb1a0843a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "03656a1f-f3fa-5cdf-b35f-3b5febfaad49" :question/math-academy-id "q-335054" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2a864f75-78c7-5949-a06f-5424af17ac17" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495196}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495196 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c02e4fa5-edc3-5680-b383-eb861b94c2ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494771} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e66a9d5-c3d1-5ab6-8270-3abb2df59cb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30dbc074-1ece-5bdf-8ee0-957449e10161" :question/math-academy-id "q-335068" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t)+7 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2fbeaf38-2336-5aee-bfc1-de7e502565a2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495181}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495250 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8628d7e9-a768-5d12-837c-9f8ec5975e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309796} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc30420-63d3-5a20-aca9-244b0f999086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310381} {:answer/id #uuid "d3937f89-bc40-5268-a944-4ae27e48a756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310452} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bbabed-8ca7-5ae8-84c8-fa65d6c477aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310694}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309796} :answer-field/id #uuid "29502f0a-5cb0-5413-af36-e8abd2820ca2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a0e04b-fdf3-54cb-b350-9898e7a963ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308813} {:answer/id #uuid "378bdb3a-aeab-5b6c-b752-3f48bb11fc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309173} {:answer/id #uuid "9af36881-ade0-5a95-98c8-166fd2c7f7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310002} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ad63a0-515c-570c-9c9a-03a0e236b3e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310316}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310002} :answer-field/id #uuid "725e744a-1eef-5fd2-950f-10310bd5d20d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311098} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ddc62a4-e5f8-5dbd-b2da-6304638bb924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309874} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c26651-816c-51dd-8978-c7e580f6e473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310202} {:answer/id #uuid "fba0073a-e68b-52d0-b4bb-84d4497e4f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310758}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310758} :answer-field/id #uuid "c81a09e8-d3d8-59a9-908d-eb56de813ddf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373d3c75-9124-5814-aa1b-1a43605c0101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309170} {:answer/id #uuid "7045fd1f-3ea6-5e00-83b9-4c746c388351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309618} {:answer/id #uuid "af797a2b-3e05-5ceb-9e14-6988ececeee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310168} {:answer/id #uuid "d765d5c4-14ae-53b0-949c-8887172f0f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310483}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310168} :answer-field/id #uuid "f916df31-d1f6-5740-aa32-119391e41ff3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "df39ea77-8f8f-5eba-a555-091c65f07d44" :question/math-academy-id "q-335404" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby  \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-At}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$"} :step/id #uuid "c5aef665-a069-598d-9521-f09b9a91fe69"}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494314}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513018} :activity/id #uuid "7fb4b445-0fd0-5c09-8ee7-7faef43b5ab2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512981 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a13ebe21-3fd3-5659-96f0-dac3aebbcdb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-e^{2t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512473}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512473} :answer-field/id #uuid "6115237a-ca95-5556-91b1-d22bf91c2c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d29ce693-46aa-5cb5-a64c-988886b4e7a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-335072" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{2t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4a313e99-6bb3-5fac-9942-cc34685e8d8e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513010}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513001 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c189b4b8-e649-59af-816a-a0162eba91e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)+{t}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370351} {:answer/id #uuid "794bd4e3-c940-5f5b-ac2e-7bed9c9fda49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370352} {:answer/id #uuid "39704c3f-642f-5f72-adf4-ba19d22ad47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/val