swer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370363} {:answer/id #uuid "313b72e4-fa0c-5a28-b44f-976590cf94a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370362} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d14676a-3691-59df-99bb-47536c494327" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c023ba-2eac-5882-bb4b-6510e186b4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370366} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bc1038-64cb-535a-b633-b2c5e10b6ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370367} {:answer/id #uuid "18d5edcb-dfe6-5a62-8079-1480a5dfcf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370367} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3847361-a50f-5b4d-82d7-e69b36f4a78c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "de398203-cf28-58bc-baf8-d4c0b37651f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-335416" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L1}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t) \\\\  & =x(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$"} :step/id #uuid "8fdaf50f-41f4-5f0b-b992-4f806b6b6092" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513012}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513010 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b374613-ddcc-5c32-8993-19ba069fb8ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{4t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512258}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512258} :answer-field/id #uuid "083c749e-9d27-588e-b8bf-03bf5d6d7291" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8c12baec-9a09-54f7-8159-4ab5ea602070" :question/math-academy-id "q-335084" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a448eb6f-7419-52b7-bf05-0c980f27a9c2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513001}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513012 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6340a434-1f61-5e6a-a285-4fc8d1b9102a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396757} {:answer/id #uuid "8b331929-7f99-5db3-bfa8-928f56ab52cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396758} {:answer/id #uuid "a9383354-b3ca-54ba-be42-38ef63dbcfa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396759} {:answer/id #uuid "11fbce92-a29e-5530-88e3-f9015373285b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396760} :answer-field/id #uuid "af7ae7ba-6ace-5d3b-a3df-d31722ff9859" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396756} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c225024-4134-558a-ac74-254995be9458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396762} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1af8f3-6b38-5b8d-bad8-3a7e70e14522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396763} {:answer/id #uuid "5381208c-3cf9-501f-8d6d-9c77cfe29564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396764} {:answer/id #uuid "c71be608-0adf-5170-8c99-84e72c9a3b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396765}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396763} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6031269-ba85-5872-aa4c-e64d608aeb30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0731d0-4386-5750-abab-d09fd58801e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396767} {:answer/id #uuid "7aebdae2-bb8c-5fcc-8f5e-cbfc865f92de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396768} {:answer/id #uuid "51ead76c-972a-53c4-aafe-40ddf79b5d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396769} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb4f772-c3f3-5eda-8d5a-76ce2843a3a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396770}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396768} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec773fb-fcb6-505d-9f93-6d40a41f5157" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e9e9aa1-972a-5335-8521-470987b0b354" :question/math-academy-id "q-335420" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$"} :step/id #uuid "b160506a-1712-5199-a906-043763a0bcdb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513018 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce80ed6-c2fb-573a-bcb7-17c24ee2cd02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512202}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d8ad94d-1b6b-50f4-917b-e60fcda59e4c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dcde9f99-5a2a-52a5-a122-c3ef3631c507" :question/math-academy-id "q-335070" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t)+1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$1-{e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t}$ </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}(-s+t+1){e}^{s-t} \\\\ {e}^{s-t}\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-(t+1){e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1-(t+1){e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-t}-t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cef7ab47-7ef6-5ce5-94ff-fd249257c533" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512981}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512086}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536011} :activity/id #uuid "12416417-305e-5bcf-9b75-2b27fd54eeed" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536011 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9104f75-3823-5343-b10e-35210deee4b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307163} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de54400-c651-59cf-a2eb-bab2e9e63b82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "411e1067-1bf2-5810-9a74-3f6443bfc23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335058" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4y(t)-4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ 1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1c1ad14e-74e6-51e6-a61f-0245fb4cfb09" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536036}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536026 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16a95f78-5388-52c8-81fd-1590793a0892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308923} {:answer/id #uuid "458cdaa3-94ab-5b93-a888-b86e89c27d0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1acb02-1114-509d-910a-98a42188ebbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309279} :answer-field/id #uuid "0676014f-804f-59e5-bdff-81ae06e0bea9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1323f90a-02bd-56b9-8366-20c0593acd49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} {:answer/id #uuid "3302abb0-2676-5e15-8a5e-e973064f4863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309136} {:answer/id #uuid "5f4876b5-f5b7-5c5b-b070-7fabe22ebc4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309463} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8dd418-5f24-589e-bdee-aad054a11f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309576}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308885} :answer-field/id #uuid "26b02ba4-09b1-554e-bc7e-4214b48c445f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89378a2d-4acc-5784-bc7b-ecf07978d854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309828} {:answer/id #uuid "9af06cd8-24db-5a45-96c2-35845daedc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} {:answer/id #uuid "b46a0660-6e5d-5316-9901-267efc99e277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310209} {:answer/id #uuid "d09ffa81-f739-5099-a822-57634e2ce021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310425}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310001} :answer-field/id #uuid "2debb7d1-7e39-57b4-b320-31d7584ebebc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310914} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b52e291-66b0-5fa6-9e5e-f2456e04f53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309073} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a78c95-4373-5610-a767-c7cb01964bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310119} {:answer/id #uuid "be64fbcf-1a13-5e30-b6c8-eb59cd744f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310287} {:answer/id #uuid "d60f5390-0372-51bc-8518-6a592260987c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310472}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309073} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bda7179-74ab-58d0-b1f2-f5c9e8cd0ec9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cebeb12c-43d2-5e26-85a3-7ca87fc81d5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335396" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby integrating both sides from $0$ to \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-At}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Integrating ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$ from $0$ to $t$ in $\\text{L3}$ yields\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSo, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by integrating both sides from $0$ to $t.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$"} :step/id #uuid "6904603d-53fd-531b-aed9-20fdeb45db7b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536050}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536029 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1e5b2a0-9a4f-5861-a763-8728282aaeea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370332} {:answer/id #uuid "e49141e3-96c9-507d-8ff6-995cb359a742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370333} {:answer/id #uuid "fafd991f-b8f7-52d0-a95d-3dd5ccc37f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370334} {:answer/id #uuid "8f7fb611-e6df-5c1b-8723-31f8eacf9ce3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370335}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370335} :answer-field/id #uuid "28cbc50b-02c4-5424-9f1b-7fce11101a13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2328997d-553e-53f3-857d-0f409d47bc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370337} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ae3eef-7d16-59e8-a6a7-53ac0338de51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370338} {:answer/id #uuid "77b7c353-0de8-54a4-b44f-0ab8d3a98105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370339} {:answer/id #uuid "0a07471f-1be3-5e6b-9c9e-47c1761506c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370340}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370339} :answer-field/id #uuid "56d1136b-14bb-539e-8254-4bd02fc30b7e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ccfd149-f7ec-54f1-a8ae-cea09d647402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370342} {:answer/id #uuid "6eedfdc4-31bc-5db4-9a15-3b9895ccc503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(0)=x(0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370343} {:answer/id #uuid "1e148004-ccba-5bcf-85ab-daff0d8a141b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370344} {:answer/id #uuid "4490b8c6-05d5-5e52-bbbb-8cca370cbec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370345}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370343} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf5e4979-0753-56be-820a-d3135a232e65" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91463c56-f813-584e-a711-1bbb5e2c2dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370347} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9771cf-2af2-5c52-924c-4e617298a6f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370348} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7938c4-9daf-50a9-843d-f8425a468cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370349}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370348} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d6f2ff9-e999-5c34-9262-e524815fe287" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "41091ce1-ce64-5374-9293-b98c681300fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-335405" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y(0)=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y(0)=x(0).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$, $\\text{L8}$, and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{At}y(t)=x(t).$"} :step/id #uuid "7a5de0ff-7990-5b8c-9f62-a36d2977e2f1"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536036 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f64bf3-528b-508d-afe7-7fb41040696f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cos(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535760} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0cddfae-ecf5-50fd-9bfc-04c2102bb55f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5cb555db-6a59-509d-947e-27c4f1a2a7e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335062" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "98ff146f-1e74-5987-92d5-7e14960c7748" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536026}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536050 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b3ed5c-fad2-5cc4-8d0b-6a6baccca373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} {:answer/id #uuid "80c6f160-e91a-566a-bbbc-ef9f781ae2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535638} {:answer/id #uuid "b43d995f-de71-5c35-a7e4-7783c88a1a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "integrating both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535711} {:answer/id #uuid "c752c0eb-512f-538b-978e-3d7df287dd00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535734}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535537} :answer-field/id #uuid "070b8c00-5b6b-5a44-a8d1-5e51fc41aa76" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8dbdd8-8dfd-5db1-b4cd-9bab37d71d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535453} {:answer/id #uuid "55d4713b-294f-5d25-89d5-a2f64e40b04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} {:answer/id #uuid "68e03ce5-612b-5030-b312-5b4ab7a5ec29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the sum rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535600} {:answer/id #uuid "864e8d51-dded-5420-af14-e1f984c4c0a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535570} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdcdafbc-2a00-5bc3-a5dd-993258a4e62f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be10430-59d1-599e-b689-c9308f9eceb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "differentiating and using the product rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b2da4-577b-58b9-8f03-aec6ff89a8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "applying a change of variables" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535547} {:answer/id #uuid "8912a77d-a8a2-5b0f-90ee-99de77bd7394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535653} {:answer/id #uuid "eda14cbf-71c6-5101-91f3-6c716e888eef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "evaluating at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535801}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535546} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1dc9399-c403-56eb-8f48-08331960ca43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ace7005c-d6c8-5219-91cc-32f47feb4972" :question/math-academy-id "q-335403" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-At}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y(0)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y(0)=x(0)$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{At}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-At})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-At}x(t)+{e}^{-At}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-At}x(t)$ at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\ny(0)={e}^{-A\\cdot 0}x(0)=Ix(0)=x(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t=0.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{At}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}y(t) & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{e}^{At}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{-As}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{At}x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{At}.$"} :step/id #uuid "f824fb6b-0584-52aa-83b5-662d7f07a788" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536029}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535426}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541191} :activity/id #uuid "4fb2a71d-ec16-5dd1-821f-b34bcd691b85" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541161 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "237ca5ab-34cd-58e7-9713-b55a6e87c11b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305489} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dd60399-b452-5b9e-ab6f-1b2c49d47ce4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752cf0f7-34a2-5108-a051-4523e28c9195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{e}^{5(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306265} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d548ec-0d73-5a36-8fa4-84091d6ec494" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cc8319e7-c74a-546c-ac46-138a893fec53" :question/math-academy-id "q-334848" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "12e96f84-4ccc-56d9-9840-fa21debf2897" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541179}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541179 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a88885-e7e0-5479-b8d2-d85e774bbf74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2s}\\cos(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540615}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540615} :answer-field/id #uuid "5681283e-4465-523e-8b0e-208f5dbcb496" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540980} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "814c0838-d0d0-5c60-bb5d-d662eb334c3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\sin(2(t-1))+\\cos(2(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540745}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540745} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f719c4-a5bf-542d-85f1-a0d87e09bdf0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b6b0c13d-ace9-58a0-a5ae-835939f481e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-334926" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">$3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1)) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-1))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -{e}^{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4e8a613a-20ab-5651-b333-3b8eba88b3c5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541213}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541183 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29953a21-209b-586e-a213-f4a4fa9d67d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305546} :answer-field/id #uuid "af02c77a-cb82-5db7-8040-47a534b70764" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "47fdaa8b-a137-5a55-9e2b-f6799e375b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-335081" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "572e3d09-d0c2-5407-860f-33864b8a2c66"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541191 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a71f00de-08de-5313-af96-a181750eb6ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2t-s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540805}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540805} :answer-field/id #uuid "665a164d-a4b1-5104-b010-c9d2e4fb6aae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba920ad2-32c3-5075-8ddb-cb1965fbe9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540840}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540840} :answer-field/id #uuid "74529953-db83-50c9-b0ad-3787b4203c7b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5195016b-d389-5c7b-a222-3fb5f86b99aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-334540" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$2t{e}^{2t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{2(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t-s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t-s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "738edf14-084a-5ae7-b9a0-e0b01debf2b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541161}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541213 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ca048f2-d590-539c-b053-4530bc08dac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^s\\cos(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540789}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540789} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eb19d6e-883e-50f6-b7d5-7815f100a541" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91956acd-af3c-5284-88d0-d96e76f54ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\sin(t-1)+3\\cos(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540772}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540772} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a78e8e2-e93a-5656-bb35-a08702392163" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed2f4962-bfe0-5321-8b55-e0e1d5307252" :question/math-academy-id "q-334928" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"190px\">$2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-1)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-1)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b57b6103-080d-5085-b5f9-fa41b8d0bc4e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541183}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540517}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557399} :activity/id #uuid "88c3f0f4-9c38-5381-bb74-2b68573561ad" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557337 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5b356a7-3b0b-5f1f-bec8-e6b826f26b86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556876}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556876} :answer-field/id #uuid "17254fb8-737c-5411-ba14-63458b8c5c1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c887629a-5ab0-5f5a-85b8-798e29da3914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556912} :answer-field/id #uuid "adcf2066-3be2-5f5c-966d-7fbfbab80820" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f491a1e5-e94d-5b1b-9331-94aa4176665c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334856" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "098818fd-a8d8-5d01-87be-46e181cc7f9d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557339}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557339 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229675 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c469a0d-2752-523c-9d5e-eb188c66277c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556717} {:answer/id #uuid "e237bdb9-b23d-538d-8ede-1bde46c2390e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556988} {:answer/id #uuid "f34842c1-f721-52e9-9b77-d0abbbd36f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557029}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556717} :answer-field/id #uuid "c47ab649-c3da-5673-8d86-71836125878a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0538cbde-d100-5661-b565-1459ce5200bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556439} {:answer/id #uuid "8271283e-49da-546a-bd56-2f6be5819b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556732} {:answer/id #uuid "b2307a16-a23b-5389-9b9e-da92d8558ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556867} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc40006-4513-51cc-b21e-641f0113825f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556924}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556439} :answer-field/id #uuid "48f44c01-f85c-5f3b-9309-7f51f9a7ace4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b327bcf-2ff8-5538-9740-b586ed698ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334922" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{5s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0df3f949-5bbe-5136-b7e7-4edc6e213b6f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557401}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557399 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "646e6165-7c3a-5090-b755-0054dbd03146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "te^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556660}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556660} :answer-field/id #uuid "174e2ccc-42c8-5609-b37a-59d23929885c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca58c0a-4a82-5bea-94ab-b3068980a554" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556855}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556855} :answer-field/id #uuid "5604af13-50f7-5867-8a20-353ebbce0164" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f8ace62-6215-5f44-93f8-e30dfc0372e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334828" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{4t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4t} & t{e}^{4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{4(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{4(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}(t-s){e}^{4t} \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dcfacae2-b140-5deb-bae8-f0b8d93c1f96" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557337}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557401 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c917360-af2a-547f-83e0-3ae046b64006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556681} {:answer/id #uuid "9a272e7c-5ccc-58a1-bc0e-68ec31a26ddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556802} {:answer/id #uuid "d2839194-a132-5ab8-875a-6230951d4cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556938} {:answer/id #uuid "e345ffd9-c7a8-5122-b489-3449540bacce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556938} :answer-field/id #uuid "46896807-998c-5933-b1eb-99ca4e046406" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b53c207-98c0-5e8d-8dea-4637e64bc338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556492} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff80451-645a-5833-911f-06d713dda45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556609} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb6b832-e503-5169-a52a-89ac629263af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556765} {:answer/id #uuid "f6eb6cc2-da68-5a29-9a26-d0470fcf0791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557041}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556609} :answer-field/id #uuid "9159810c-d2c6-59d8-84ab-dc3766a59aa8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e6e37b0-420c-5604-b7d4-9e71462bd5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-334923" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">$2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">${e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-1))+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-1))\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{6s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "de6d93f6-e851-58c8-a9b2-117e1ba0ae41"}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556414}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671} :activity/id #uuid "10f6eef1-5078-55a6-b949-5b4bf786db94" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "160b514e-c7a9-5db1-8962-33d86d078fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305342} :answer-field/id #uuid "63437be9-2066-5dad-a01a-a0e02722c169" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05184db4-a95b-5878-863f-1aa2b4e40630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305198} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1530c65-7d45-5311-814a-529b693ace24" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7aef4d9e-5adf-5d9d-be87-6231a093c423" :question/math-academy-id "q-334855" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3cf553b5-a0c0-5e03-adcb-b5e28abcb810" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325e2bea-79c6-5d0e-86e5-ca3c08841f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557971} {:answer/id #uuid "8e624ff8-2ee1-5b70-ba81-5895a41c4248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558145} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ecf254-834a-5dbe-8b2d-44e08553fb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} {:answer/id #uuid "f6893209-e8c4-5a46-9f8a-822f69bcdaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t+s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558350}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558228} :answer-field/id #uuid "dadfc882-5148-5c0c-af21-a9e418a22bd6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558464} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69fe7ba5-1b53-56bf-9a9f-f5c568562239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6829ae-e7c1-5884-afa0-116dfe94231c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558142} {:answer/id #uuid "ad7f1da6-be8e-55ae-86e2-b2f30e2b8500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558212} {:answer/id #uuid "c87fcfa6-f6e3-5441-b2a1-174c935027eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558267}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558069} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffb55f3c-2681-5734-9a74-f7bf06c53fcc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cb2daa37-d9b1-570d-9a42-38ab64cc0e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-334859" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}} </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8b6c1363-f2b6-518d-a59c-19b0d9f1d213"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59687fe-7fee-536b-ae53-62aa4e2062c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558287} :answer-field/id #uuid "bda1e7e4-3c88-5a06-909e-308c1b22da65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eb1113-b696-53f5-ab1f-005ae9690189" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc834a44-d315-5323-8d37-5104d3268aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-334846" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a7f36150-a323-543f-a05f-ad14ac2a2c6c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558616}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557852}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046673} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570849} :activity/id #uuid "8d3adf3f-e138-58ac-be7c-f8a39b171e26" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050707 :topic/id #uuid "605a21e1-c415-5cc1-9181-c8f48db5f4ba" :topic/math-academy-id 6691} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570813 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b12c1e03-c805-5e36-aea2-b6d121e73478" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306815} {:answer/id #uuid "74474233-2fa8-51ba-9cb4-da5296695f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\cos(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479536} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f5abdf-75a7-5b21-afa3-653d497c5d41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab25cf3f-5e10-5e03-b9ec-f148d948ee64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306768} {:answer/id #uuid "677ff288-ab7f-56c0-a677-5f7330959d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\cos(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479513} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9d3c90-4891-5e53-85e9-0abe74fcc6f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c3b7f24-1005-522b-87d6-a7afb67ecc23" :question/math-academy-id "q-334858" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3faafc6b-71b5-511b-9711-f9114709af7a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570837}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570829 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396565 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "445c6a63-f339-5ff2-afa4-e26785fbf1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396567} {:answer/id #uuid "96de3917-2210-5111-9750-f9437e72cfa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} {:answer/id #uuid "875915a9-2dd7-5bfd-a876-9d427aa8a55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396569} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2a0cc9-e777-59ad-9b3f-6332bbbb90e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396570}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396568} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c7d9a-e955-5ffd-bbe8-c5635e09bdc8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d2b8ad61-9b47-5971-9495-e31b2ea4691b" :question/math-academy-id "q-335175" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+2,\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6996d827-5862-511f-81db-81953235cdc4"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570837 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1469716d-c345-5ffe-8890-e1981e80d56a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479390} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5c4e43-e417-5c07-a2c3-eb9628d96e3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)-3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479445} {:answer/id #uuid "740b8e1d-0233-597c-ac41-6431abd888f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479535} {:answer/id #uuid "deba3bee-d355-5039-ab99-fbef85ee9df4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479535} :answer-field/id #uuid "4952d3ec-dd70-5ca3-b11d-7bddbd2cbfa1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13688bbb-8a94-53d1-b777-8b7a97c5b5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479387} {:answer/id #uuid "76d12e8f-d604-5766-8275-33330f073e0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479538} {:answer/id #uuid "c13c88e1-4c54-5e6c-a695-0823d83ecac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479648} {:answer/id #uuid "e7edf428-062b-5000-bf1d-efff0567c499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t+s))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479702}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479538} :answer-field/id #uuid "d776bb26-ce4b-5844-8f89-c1e2c8830a03" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "462afb47-f28d-50fb-a384-b84e85e58f07" :question/math-academy-id "q-334920" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{4t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"160px\">${e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s))$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4t)+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-s)) \\\\ {e}^{4s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-s))\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7fcb2994-7f35-5585-b8ef-6c814be8d434" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570858}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570849 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4bfced-4c23-541f-b242-4c2ea02d35eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306347} {:answer/id #uuid "72e16707-4ff3-5dfd-9eed-366cbfa6fe18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479531} :answer-field/id #uuid "52d98b8a-0ce9-5cfa-a498-ed17c16b2e6d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1c22720-1aa8-597e-9b76-8432cec4de4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307375} {:answer/id #uuid "27dc7621-01eb-5ac6-8247-fe730465d634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479418} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba95706-4eaf-526e-986f-73babc57c464" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "001f1d7b-e465-5a31-aa71-fce5efbdd939" :question/math-academy-id "q-334824" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$(t-s){e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ {e}^{3s}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}(t-s){e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ab6e41fa-e577-543c-8c44-dd8e57314fc7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570813}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570858 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8e79b01-2389-5a91-bd1b-47d545c124e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307021} {:answer/id #uuid "06fe7ba9-e60a-5a45-b758-fa0196ee521e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{5t}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479370} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1add94-bde4-538a-ae6f-d06b8a3019c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19468931-2ce6-5bd0-af7b-5212e5297c87" :question/math-academy-id "q-335085" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5t}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c8fbc123-cd40-50c1-9ac9-254d6e8dd576" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570829}}] :activity/title "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570106}]}
